argest eigenvalue of the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$ \n\nThe square roots of the eigenvalues of ${A}^{T}A$ are called the *singular values* of $A.$ Since the largest singular value of $A$ is ${\\sigma }_{1}=9,$ the largest eigenvalue of ${A}^{T}A$ must be ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}={9}^{2}.$ So, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax{‖}^{2}}={9}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}{‖Ax‖}=9.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is ${\\sigma }_{1}=9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139535/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd0e91f0-abbc-52e2-8d8b-94597e4892cd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139535"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection/2fb71e7ac9a746d46f20e98e6b1d4cc4cfc6391b47f1e1b0a4d87f422531279c" :answer/id #uuid "893a1fd4-dd04-5d61-825f-3238c36570aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{v}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection/9a867eacbef27445c44cc2ed4a7455cb26ab606739712a93b4d78bec8792e363" :answer/id #uuid "843a20c9-138e-525a-9418-f666bbcc865e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{v}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection/1af1fa63e339904075f5bb159186d4e5f4548be7cd5339d60ffc906a0e28a7f3" :answer/id #uuid "6c567e06-ce1b-58c1-b562-0bdd3f09301c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection/b629d18601f69b06f4b720019656d7c15680090caad1ea634753312f5dc6a33d" :answer/id #uuid "9c42ac91-c71d-53ef-9489-6d23e663db65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{A}^{T}{v}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection/0e72a2ffb412c78686d4274f6db2f95f386959f0a6aae3c4356f8daaa24b476b" :answer/id #uuid "f5a8f5c3-184d-54b3-89ed-67313be48478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf47af50-04f0-5984-8c12-cf81a141857e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139555/selection/0e72a2ffb412c78686d4274f6db2f95f386959f0a6aae3c4356f8daaa24b476b" :answer-field/choices ["q-139555/selection/2fb71e7ac9a746d46f20e98e6b1d4cc4cfc6391b47f1e1b0a4d87f422531279c" "q-139555/selection/9a867eacbef27445c44cc2ed4a7455cb26ab606739712a93b4d78bec8792e363" "q-139555/selection/1af1fa63e339904075f5bb159186d4e5f4548be7cd5339d60ffc906a0e28a7f3" "q-139555/selection/b629d18601f69b06f4b720019656d7c15680090caad1ea634753312f5dc6a33d" "q-139555/selection/0e72a2ffb412c78686d4274f6db2f95f386959f0a6aae3c4356f8daaa24b476b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139555" :question/id #uuid "92d0f016-ed66-5b4a-b12a-1eb9f25bd4fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-139555" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/assets/2d1cefc0c789518d21279c5c49a18f80220a2aad80973f0e84fda0ddaf25493b.png)\n\nA $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ maps the unit circle ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{2}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ which of the following is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $100$ of ${A}^{T}A?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=10={\\sigma }_{1},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{1}={10}^{2}=100,$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=8={\\sigma }_{2},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{2}={8}^{2}=64.$\n\nTherefore, an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=100$ of ${A}^{T}A$ is ${v}_{1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139555/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cec3c21-28df-52ba-9b78-86cffb4c7720"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139555"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-139421"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14077831/assets/f26e876d5234313926a2cbaa8938e32c8a725cf3435ce3113361bfa3dc1b7997.png)\n\nA $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ maps the unit circle ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{2}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ which of the following is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $25$ of ${A}^{T}A?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=7={\\sigma }_{1},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{1}={7}^{2}=49,$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=5={\\sigma }_{2},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{2}={5}^{2}=25.$\n\nTherefore, an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=25$ of ${A}^{T}A$ is ${v}_{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection/8344a2db21bf14088ac3c80e02c15906132c1d4539abda94d195a84eccd21792" :answer/id #uuid "9954fd72-21d7-5a0e-a582-737da4fc5d00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9{v}_{1}$ and $4{v}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection/f43f6539d74d260a043f1d9c62ee7a42c7418ec27eb5ac28f6fafc0de6585102" :answer/id #uuid "1c85c95b-b2bf-5fbb-b70a-9bf0921be222" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ and $8$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection/9c4a0945dd545ed7e97f85a7363b07ec888f53f7bb1fdc948795cfc938eba2e0" :answer/id #uuid "631a5204-d6f9-5fc9-8461-c8a19b8b90f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection/67cb1be3333a3e5358177cb47769fab9690031e0294337deafaceade6cce27d9" :answer/id #uuid "320776f1-04d7-5383-b61f-87392a009131" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{1}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection/1d708705be678df4ad4cd332dcc8f653a0b02c4827e3588ca8917b08b2a46a25" :answer/id #uuid "1dc673c8-c739-53db-88ba-5fef92319e4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ee72b0-4f56-5a0b-b64e-262fd9cc37d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139550/selection/1d708705be678df4ad4cd332dcc8f653a0b02c4827e3588ca8917b08b2a46a25" :answer-field/choices ["q-139550/selection/8344a2db21bf14088ac3c80e02c15906132c1d4539abda94d195a84eccd21792" "q-139550/selection/f43f6539d74d260a043f1d9c62ee7a42c7418ec27eb5ac28f6fafc0de6585102" "q-139550/selection/9c4a0945dd545ed7e97f85a7363b07ec888f53f7bb1fdc948795cfc938eba2e0" "q-139550/selection/67cb1be3333a3e5358177cb47769fab9690031e0294337deafaceade6cce27d9" "q-139550/selection/1d708705be678df4ad4cd332dcc8f653a0b02c4827e3588ca8917b08b2a46a25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139550" :question/id #uuid "f3e183c0-f2c5-57a2-8b6d-